          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JCSM7HHJrSrdpx8GARGdxn",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: Centralizing both credential injection and runtime path resolution to a single decision point, reducing surface area for misconfiguration and unauthorized access.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - pattern/Composition\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both credential-scoping and runtime-paths explicitly apply this pattern; pages are consistent and detailed enough that the connection is direct.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2027-01-14\\n---\\n\\nGrimoire\u0027s architecture applies a **single composition point** principle to both\\ncredentials and file-system paths. Rather than allowing these to be discovered,\\nresolved, or injected at many different points in the codebase, both concerns are\\nrouted through a single, validated decision point at startup or process spawn.\\n\\n## Credentials: Single Injection Point\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] centralizes the injection of the Anthropic API key into child\\nprocesses. The Hub process never holds the key itself; a local secrets loader reads it\\nfrom a \u0060.env\u0060 file and injects it into the environment of the Ingest and Query agent\\nchild processes immediately before they spawn. This means a compromised Hub process\\ncannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment \u2014 the key exists only in\\nthe short-lived child process that actually uses it.\\n\\n## File-System Paths: Single Resolution Point\\n\\n[[runtime-paths]] centralizes the resolution of all runtime file-system locations\\n(wiki content root, data directory, SQLite database, secrets file, agent instruction\\ndirectories) into a single path resolver at Hub startup. No other part of the codebase\\nreads the ambient working directory directly; everything downstream consumes the\\nalready-resolved path set instead.\\n\\n## The Pattern\\n\\nBoth decisions apply the same principle: **eliminate scattered decision points in favor\\nof a single authoritative composition**. This reduces the surface area for:\\n- Misconfiguration (only one place to get right)\\n- Unauthorized access or mutation (only one place to control)\\n- Debugging and auditing (one place to inspect the effective configuration)\\n\\nWhen a new requirement arrives \u2014 a new agent, a new secret type, a new data directory \u2014\\nthe pattern is already clear: extend the single composition point, not scatter new\\nlogic across the codebase.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
